# React Component Conventions

## Dashboard Panels (`components/dashboard/`)

Each panel corresponds to one item in the 14-step analysis checklist:

1. SessionHeader — car, track, driver, conditions
2. LapTimesChart — per-lap times with max speed
3. TyreTempsPanel — surface temps (O/M/I) per corner per lap
4. TyrePressuresChart — hot pressures per corner per lap
5. TyreWearPanel — tread remaining per corner
6. ConditioningTrend — temp conditioning rate over stint
7. RideHeightScatter — ride heights at speed
8. SplitterAnalysis — center front splitter ride height
9. ShockVelocityPanel — shock velocity stats (p95, p99, peak)
10. GForceScatter — lateral vs longitudinal g scatter
11. EngineTempsPanel — water and oil temps per lap
12. FuelPanel — consumption rate and range
13. DriverAidsPanel — brake bias, TC, ABS changes
14. RARBAnalysis — front/rear ARB blade analysis
15. SetupDump — raw setup YAML display

### Panel Pattern

```tsx
import { Card } from '../shared/Card';
import type { SessionAnalysis } from '../../lib/types';

interface Props {
  analysis: SessionAnalysis;
}

export function PanelName({ analysis }: Props) {
  // Destructure what you need from analysis
  // Use Card wrapper with title and icon
  return (
    <Card title="Panel Title" icon="🔧">
      {/* content */}
    </Card>
  );
}
```

### Rules
- Always accept `analysis: SessionAnalysis` as the prop.
- Wrap content in the `Card` component from `../shared/Card`.
- Use `StatusBadge` for threshold-based status indicators (COLD/OK/HOT/HIGH/SAFE/RISK).
- Use `MetricRow` for label/value pairs with optional units and status.
- Use thresholds from `src/lib/constants.ts` — never hardcode threshold values.
- Recharts charts use colors from the `COLORS` constant.

## Shared Components (`components/shared/`)

- `Card` — Panel container with title, icon, optional grid span.
- `TabBar` — Tab navigation for the dashboard sections.
- `StatusBadge` — Colored status pill (uses `STATUS_COLORS` mapping).
- `MetricRow` — Single metric display: label, value, unit, status.

Keep shared components generic — no telemetry-specific logic in shared components.
